01:01:35,109 --> 01:01:36,277
Millburn.

800
01:01:36,443 --> 01:01:38,445
What's all this black stuff?

801
01:01:41,448 --> 01:01:43,868
Hm. Gazpacho.

802
01:01:46,453 --> 01:01:47,454
Is that tobacco?

803
01:01:48,330 --> 01:01:49,248
Is that tobacco...

804
01:01:49,415 --> 01:01:50,541
...in your respirator?

805
01:01:50,708 --> 01:01:52,293
Yeah, sure.

806
01:01:56,797 --> 01:01:58,632
- Tobacco.
- Heh-heh-heh.

807
01:01:58,966 --> 01:02:02,595
On behalf of scientists everywhere,
I am ashamed to count you amongst us...

808
01:02:02,761 --> 01:02:04,388
...Fifield. Really.

809
01:02:08,642 --> 01:02:09,727
- Hey, Millburn.
- Yeah?

810
01:02:09,894 --> 01:02:10,811
You see this thing?

811
01:02:10,978 --> 01:02:14,315
What do you think this thing was?
Some kind of a god?

812
01:02:14,815 --> 01:02:16,817
Something they worshiped?
What?

813
01:02:16,984 --> 01:02:18,736
- It kind of looks like...
- What's that?

814
01:02:19,445 --> 01:02:20,487
What the hell is that?

815
01:02:20,654 --> 01:02:21,906
Oh, my God. Okay.

816
01:02:22,072 --> 01:02:23,407
Just stay calm. Stay quiet.

817
01:02:23,574 --> 01:02:25,826
This is okay, I can handle this.

818
01:02:26,493 --> 01:02:27,494
Hey, baby.

819
01:02:28,287 --> 01:02:28,996
Hey.

820
01:02:29,997 --> 01:02:31,165
Uh, come in, <i>Prometheus</i>.

821
01:02:31,498 --> 01:02:35,085
<i>We have an elongate
reptile-type creature.</i>

822
01:02:35,294 --> 01:02:39,423
<i>Maybe 30, 40 inches,
with transparent skin.</i>

823
01:02:39,840 --> 01:02:41,175
And it's beautiful.

824
01:02:42,843 --> 01:02:43,344
Okay!

825
01:02:43,510 --> 01:02:45,429
Hoo-hoo-hoo. Hoo!

826
01:02:46,805 --> 01:02:47,431
<i>Prometheus</i>...

827
01:02:47,598 --> 01:02:48,349
...we have two.

828
01:02:48,515 --> 01:02:51,018
Look at you. Look at you, baby.

829
01:02:51,518 --> 01:02:53,979
Jesus, look at the size of that.
What is it?

830
01:02:54,146 --> 01:02:56,690
- You need to stay calm.
- What's there to be calm about?

831
01:02:56,857 --> 01:02:59,276
You need to stay calm
because she is beautiful.

832
01:02:59,443 --> 01:03:01,195
What makes you think that's female?

833
01:03:01,362 --> 01:03:02,613
She's a lady. Look! Hm?

834
01:03:07,242 --> 01:03:09,703
Ah. Hey.

835
01:03:10,579 --> 01:03:11,622
She's mesmerized.

836
01:03:12,039 --> 01:03:14,166
Come here. Come here.

837
01:03:16,418 --> 01:03:17,544
It's okay.

838
01:03:17,711 --> 01:03:19,380
It's okay. It's okay.

839
01:03:20,089 --> 01:03:21,382
Hey, baby.

840
01:03:24,551 --> 01:03:25,469
You're strong!

841
01:03:26,220 --> 01:03:26,845
You should...

842
01:03:27,012 --> 01:03:27,680
...help me now.

843
01:03:27,846 --> 01:03:28,514
Get it off!

844
01:03:29,348 --> 01:03:30,224
Aah!

845
01:03:31,100 --> 01:03:31,976
Cut it here, man!

846
01:03:32,142 --> 01:03:33,227
I ain't touching that!

847
01:03:34,228 --> 01:03:36,230
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

848
01:03:36,397 --> 01:03:38,440
- It's getting tighter.
- I ain't touching it.

849
01:03:38,607 --> 01:03:41,402
Cut the thing, man, for God's sake! Aah!

850
01:03:41,568 --> 01:03:43,487
God, you're making it worse! Aah!

851
01:03:43,654 --> 01:03:45,698
It's tightening! It's tight...
Aah, aah!

852
01:03:45,864 --> 01:03:47,074
It's breaking my arm!

853
01:03:48,993 --> 01:03:49,576
Shit!

854
01:03:49,994 --> 01:03:50,869
Cut it off!

855
01:03:51,036 --> 01:03:52,746
Cut it off!

856
01:03:52,913 --> 01:03:53,747
Cut it off!

857
01:03:53,914 --> 01:03:54,540
Cut it off!

858
01:03:57,543 --> 01:03:58,168
Shit!

859
01:03:58,335 --> 01:03:59,086
Oh, my God!

860
01:04:00,379 --> 01:04:02,423
Oh, my God! Oh, Jesus!

861
01:04:03,841 --> 01:04:05,092
It's in my suit.

862
01:04:05,259 --> 01:04:06,051
Jesus Christ.

863
01:05:06,153 --> 01:05:07,988
<i>Shaw, you up?</i>

864
01:05:09,656 --> 01:05:10,824
Yeah, what's up?

865
01:05:11,200 --> 01:05:13,410
<i>The storm passed,
but I can't reach Millburn...</i>

866
01:05:13,577 --> 01:05:16,789
<i>...or Fifield. Taking a few men down,
see if I can rustle them up.</i>

867
01:05:16,955 --> 01:05:18,082
Okay.

868
01:05:18,999 --> 01:05:20,584
Uh, any idea where they are?

869
01:05:20,751 --> 01:05:24,421
Last time they radioed in was
where you found your head.

870
01:05:24,963 --> 01:05:26,924
<i>Okay, we're coming.</i>

871
01:05:27,091 --> 01:05:27,841
All right.

872
01:05:28,008 --> 01:05:30,844
Chance, you're coming with me. Come on.

873
01:05:31,011 --> 01:05:32,012
All right, boss.

874
01:05:33,847 --> 01:05:36,642
- Ravel, did you fix that glitch?
- <i>No, captain.</i>

875
01:05:36,809 --> 01:05:39,561
- <i>It's gotta be in the hardware.</i>
- What glitch, captain?

876
01:05:39,728 --> 01:05:42,272
One of them probes picked up a life form.

877
01:05:42,981 --> 01:05:43,941
Pops up every hour...

878
01:05:44,108 --> 01:05:47,027
...for a couple of seconds
and then it's gone.

879
01:05:47,194 --> 01:05:48,779
I can find the probe and fix it.

880
01:05:48,946 --> 01:05:50,531
Knock yourself out.

881
01:05:51,865 --> 01:05:53,367
Be careful, doctors.

882
01:06:14,596 --> 01:06:16,348
Fifield!

883
01:06:19,101 --> 01:06:20,269
Millburn?

884
01:06:24,565 --> 01:06:25,941
All right, come on down.

885
01:06:46,962 --> 01:06:49,923
<i>David, are you alone?</i>

886
01:06:51,049 --> 01:06:52,176
Yes, Miss Vickers.

887
01:06:52,342 --> 01:06:54,511
<i>Uplink your feed to my room.</i>

888
01:06:54,678 --> 01:06:55,971
Copy.

889
01:08:38,573 --> 01:08:40,784
You son of a bitch.

890
01:08:42,869 --> 01:08:44,579
You cut me off.

891
01:09:05,684 --> 01:09:07,227
What is this?

892
01:09:10,731 --> 01:09:11,940
- Charlie?
- I just tripped.

893
01:09:12,232 --> 01:09:13,400
Oh, my God, you're sick.

894
01:09:13,567 --> 01:09:15,485
I'm okay, baby. Come on.

895
01:09:15,652 --> 01:09:16,695
Fifield?

896
01:09:17,529 --> 01:09:18,739
Millburn?

897
01:09:25,203 --> 01:09:26,747
Hey, Chance. I wouldn't touch...

898
01:09:26,913 --> 01:09:28,081
...that if I were you.

899
01:09:30,959 --> 01:09:32,294
Dr. Shaw?

900
01:09:32,461 --> 01:09:33,587
Yeah?

901
01:09:33,754 --> 01:09:35,756
Do we have any idea what is...

902
01:09:35,922 --> 01:09:37,341
...oozing out of these vases?

903
01:09:37,507 --> 01:09:40,677
No. They weren't like this
last time we were here.

904
01:09:45,390 --> 01:09:46,516
Captain?

905
01:09:46,725 --> 01:09:48,018
What?

906
01:09:48,226 --> 01:09:49,186
Who is it? Which one?

907
01:09:49,353 --> 01:09:51,188
- Who is it?
- It's Millburn.

908
01:09:51,730 --> 01:09:53,607
- Ellie.
- Don't touch him. Hold on.

909
01:09:53,774 --> 01:09:54,608
Ellie, honey.

910
01:09:54,775 --> 01:09:56,610
Charlie, what's wrong?

911
01:09:56,777 --> 01:09:59,321
I need you to look at me, okay?

912
01:09:59,488 --> 01:10:00,614
You know infections...

913
01:10:00,781 --> 01:10:01,823
...so, what do you see?

914
01:10:01,990 --> 01:10:03,617
This is not good, baby.

915
01:10:03,784 --> 01:10:05,702
You look at me,
you tell me what you see.

916
01:10:07,621 --> 01:10:08,789
Aah!

917
01:10:09,956 --> 01:10:10,832
Oh, my God.

918
01:10:11,291 --> 01:10:12,876
Ford, get over here.

919
01:10:13,043 --> 01:10:14,628
It's okay. Janek?

920
01:10:14,795 --> 01:10:16,421
- What?
- We have to go now!

921
01:10:16,588 --> 01:10:17,297
What do you see?

922
01:10:17,464 --> 01:10:19,466
Honey, what do you see?

923
01:10:19,633 --> 01:10:21,718
Holloway's sick. He's not good.

924
01:10:21,885 --> 01:10:22,469
I see movement...

925
01:10:22,636 --> 01:10:23,303
...in his esophagus.

926
01:10:27,641 --> 01:10:29,309
- Come on, baby.
- No. I'm okay.

927
01:10:29,476 --> 01:10:30,435
Janek!

928
01:10:30,602 --> 01:10:31,812
Come over and help me!

929
01:10:31,978 --> 01:10:34,314
- I'm okay.
- Ford, get over. What's happening?

930
01:10:34,481 --> 01:10:35,482
- I'm okay.
- Let's go!

931
01:10:35,649 --> 01:10:36,775
Help me with him.

932
01:10:36,942 --> 01:10:39,820
I got you.
We're gonna get you out of here.

933
01:10:39,986 --> 01:10:40,654
<i>Prometheus</i>...

934
01:10:40,821 --> 01:10:41,446
...come in.

935
01:10:41,613 --> 01:10:43,573
- Watch your head.
- Okay. I'm okay.

936
01:10:43,740 --> 01:10:45,492
- Holloway.
- Get him up.

937
01:10:45,659 --> 01:10:47,494
- Come on.
- <i>Prometheus</i>, come in.

938
01:10:47,661 --> 01:10:48,829
<i>Is anyone there?</i>

939
01:10:49,496 --> 01:10:50,747
This is Vickers.

940
01:10:50,914 --> 01:10:53,375
I need a medical team
standing by the airlock.

941
01:10:53,708 --> 01:10:55,752
<i>Full quarantine fail-safe.</i>

942
01:10:55,919 --> 01:10:57,379
<i>Holloway's sick.</i>

943
01:10:57,546 --> 01:10:58,797
Sick with what?

944
01:10:58,964 --> 01:11:01,091
- Just do it.
- Let's get him back to the ship.

945
01:11:01,258 --> 01:11:03,343
- <i>It's not safe down here.</i>
- <i>Charlie?</i>

946
01:11:03,510 --> 01:11:04,344
I'm suiting up.

947
01:11:04,511 --> 01:11:06,179
- <i>Charlie, talk to me.</i>
- <i>Move!</i>

948
01:11:06,346 --> 01:11:08,682
- <i>What was that back there?</i>
- <i>Let's go, people!</i>

949
01:11:10,392 --> 01:11:12,644
<i>We've gotta move!
We've gotta move!</i>

950
01:11:12,811 --> 01:11:13,395
<i>Ellie!</i>

951
01:15:11,091 --> 01:15:12,300
He don't look too good.

952
01:15:12,509 --> 01:15:15,220
Did he catch something down there?
We had our helmets off.

953
01:15:15,387 --> 01:15:16,096
I don't know.

954
01:15:16,388 --> 01:15:19,391
<i>Prometheus</i>, this is Janek.
Make sure that back door is open.

955
01:15:19,766 --> 01:15:20,850
<i>Aye, captain.</i>

956
01:15:21,017 --> 01:15:23,395
Oh, God. I'm so sorry.

957
01:15:25,105 --> 01:15:26,356
Come on!

958
01:15:26,523 --> 01:15:28,233
Please!

959
01:15:33,071 --> 01:15:35,573
<i>Prometheus!</i>
Why is that door not open?

960
01:15:36,116 --> 01:15:37,951
Vickers, that is an order!

961
01:15:38,743 --> 01:15:40,370
Get that goddamn door open!

962
01:15:40,537 --> 01:15:43,081
- Look at me. It's too late, I'm sick.
- No, it's not.

963
01:15:43,248 --> 01:15:44,457
Come on!

964
01:15:45,166 --> 01:15:45,875
Ford, help me!

965
01:15:46,251 --> 01:15:48,294
Airlock crew, if you can hear me, it's Janek.

966
01:15:48,461 --> 01:15:50,088
<i>Open that back door right now!</i>

967
01:15:50,255 --> 01:15:51,423
Hold that door!

968
01:15:51,589 --> 01:15:52,257
Prometheus<i>...</i>

969
01:15:52,424 --> 01:15:53,174
<i>...do you copy?</i>

970
01:15:53,341 --> 01:15:55,844
<i>Goddamn it, open that door!
That is an order!</i>

971
01:15:56,010 --> 01:15:57,095
Open it.

972
01:16:04,144 --> 01:16:05,437
What the hell is this?

973
01:16:05,603 --> 01:16:07,147
He's not coming on board.

974
01:16:07,313 --> 01:16:08,815
Vickers, this is a sick man.

975
01:16:08,982 --> 01:16:10,108
I see that. That's why...

976
01:16:10,275 --> 01:16:11,317
...he's not coming on!

977
01:16:11,484 --> 01:16:13,111
- Aah!
- Charlie!

978
01:16:13,278 --> 01:16:14,320
Chance, get over here!

979
01:16:17,615 --> 01:16:18,324
Please!

980
01:16:18,491 --> 01:16:19,576
We can still help him!

981
01:16:21,244 --> 01:16:23,830
Help yourself.
Everybody but Holloway back on this ship!

982
01:16:23,997 --> 01:16:25,582
I won't leave him!

983
01:16:25,749 --> 01:16:26,583
Then stay!

984
01:16:26,750 --> 01:16:27,917
Wait! We could...

985
01:16:28,084 --> 01:16:29,794
...put him on the Med-Pod!

986
01:16:29,961 --> 01:16:31,004
Please don't do this.

987
01:16:31,171 --> 01:16:32,505
It's okay, Ellie.

988
01:16:32,672 --> 01:16:33,673
Vickers!

989
01:16:33,840 --> 01:16:34,841
What are you doing?

990
01:16:35,133 --> 01:16:36,301
I love you, baby.

991
01:16:36,468 --> 01:16:37,302
- I love you.
- No.

992
01:16:37,469 --> 01:16:38,762
I'm telling you, stay back!

993
01:16:38,928 --> 01:16:39,637
Do it.

994
01:16:39,804 --> 01:16:40,680
Stay back!

995
01:16:40,847 --> 01:16:41,931
No! No, Charlie!

996
01:16:42,098 --> 01:16:42,682
- Do it.
- No!

997
01:16:48,438 --> 01:16:49,647
No!

998
01:16:51,691 --> 01:16:53,193
No!

999
01:16:53,526 --> 01:16:55,195
No!

1000
01:16:58,865 --> 01:16:59,949
Charlie!

1001
01:17:02,702 --> 01:17:04,329
No!

1002
01:17:17,717 --> 01:17:19,677
My deepest condolences.

1003
01:17:21,012 --> 01:17:22,806
I'm going to have to take this.

1004
01:17:22,972 --> 01:17:24,516
It may be contaminated.

1005
01:17:25,642 --> 01:17:29,687
If there's a contagion,
we were all exposed.

1006
01:17:31,272 --> 01:17:35,068
You need... We need to run blood work
on everyone who set foot in the pyramid.

1007
01:17:35,735 --> 01:17:37,111
Yes, of course.

1008
01:17:37,403 --> 01:17:38,696
Yes?

1009
01:17:46,037 --> 01:17:48,414
I understand how...

1010
01:17:48,581 --> 01:17:50,083
...inappropriate this is...

1011
01:17:50,875 --> 01:17:53,211
...given the circumstances.

1012
01:17:53,378 --> 01:17:56,381
But as you ordered
quarantine fail-safes...

1013
01:17:58,216 --> 01:18:00,510
...it's my responsibility to ask.

1014
01:18:01,427 --> 01:18:05,598
Have you and Dr. Holloway had
any intimate contact recently?

1015
01:18:06,933 --> 01:18:08,101
Since you and he were...

1016
01:18:08,268 --> 01:18:09,519
...so close...

1017
01:18:10,436 --> 01:18:11,271
...I want to be...

1018
01:18:11,437 --> 01:18:12,897
...as thorough as poss...

1019
01:18:14,899 --> 01:18:15,733
My, my.

1020
01:18:19,946 --> 01:18:20,822
You're pregnant.

1021
01:18:23,700 --> 01:18:24,367
What?

1022
01:18:25,869 --> 01:18:27,620
From the look of it, three months so.

1023
01:18:28,079 --> 01:18:31,165
No, that's impossible.

1024
01:18:31,457 --> 01:18:33,585
I can't be pregnant.

1025
01:18:33,877 --> 01:18:37,213
Did you have intercourse
with Dr. Holloway?

1026
01:18:38,047 --> 01:18:39,257
Yes...

1027
01:18:39,424 --> 01:18:42,468
...but 10 hours ago.

1028
01:18:42,802 --> 01:18:46,306
There's no bloody way I'm
three months pregnant.

1029
01:18:46,472 --> 01:18:47,307
Well, doctor...

1030
01:18:48,308 --> 01:18:50,393
...it's not exactly a traditional fetus.

1031
01:18:54,105 --> 01:18:54,981
I want to see it.

1032
01:18:55,273 --> 01:18:56,983
Don't think that's a good idea.

1033
01:18:58,818 --> 01:19:01,654
David, I want to see it.

1034
01:19:01,946 --> 01:19:03,156
Now, doctor...

1035
01:19:05,658 --> 01:19:07,160
I want to see it.

1036
01:19:08,244 --> 01:19:09,662
I want it out of me.

1037
01:19:09,913 --> 01:19:11,497
We don't have the personnel...

1038
01:19:11,664 --> 01:19:14,167
...to perform a procedure like that.

1039
01:19:14,334 --> 01:19:16,169
- Our best option...
- I want it out.

1040
01:19:16,336 --> 01:19:17,337
Put you back into...

1041
01:19:17,503 --> 01:19:19,422
...cryostasis until we return to Earth.

1042
01:19:19,589 --> 01:19:21,883
Please, get it out of me.

1043
01:19:22,216 --> 01:19:23,635
Get it out of me!

1044
01:19:23,927 --> 01:19:25,011
Please.

1045
01:19:28,640 --> 01:19:30,350
It must be very painful.

1046
01:19:31,225 --> 01:19:33,353
Here, let me give you something.

1047
01:19:37,357 --> 01:19:39,025
That's it. There, there.

1048
01:19:45,448 --> 01:19:48,034
Someone will be along shortly...

1049
01:19:48,326 --> 01:19:50,703
...to bring you back to Cryo Deck.

1050
01:19:54,999 --> 01:19:57,251
It must feel like your God abandoned you.

1051
01:19:57,877 --> 01:19:59,045
What?

1052
01:19:59,212 --> 01:20:00,004
To lose...

1053
01:20:00,171 --> 01:20:04,884
...Dr. Holloway after your father died
under such similar circumstances.

1054
01:20:05,468 --> 01:20:07,553
What was it that killed him?

1055
01:20:08,304 --> 01:20:09,764
Ebola?

1056
01:20:14,143 --> 01:20:16,896
How do you...? How do you know that?

1057
01:20:18,022 --> 01:20:19,816
I watched your dreams.

1058
01:20:42,380 --> 01:20:43,464
Dr. Shaw?

1059
01:20:44,757 --> 01:20:45,925
We're here to put you...

1060
01:20:46,092 --> 01:20:49,470
...in an anti-contamination suit,
take you back to Cryo Deck...

1061
01:20:49,637 --> 01:20:51,264
...go to beddy-byes.

1062
01:20:51,931 --> 01:20:53,433
Dr. Shaw?

1063
01:20:54,934 --> 01:20:56,394
She's doped. Prepare her.

1064
01:21:26,424 --> 01:21:28,593
<i>Emergency procedures initiated.</i>

1065
01:21:28,760 --> 01:21:30,636
<i>Please verbally state
the nature of your injury.</i>

1066
01:21:31,345 --> 01:21:33,264
I need a Caesarean.

1067
01:21:33,806 --> 01:21:35,975
<i>Error. This Med-Pod
is calibrated for male...</i>

1068
01:21:36,142 --> 01:21:37,727
<i>...patients and does not offer...</i>

1069
01:21:37,894 --> 01:21:40,813
<i>...the procedure you have requested.
Seek medical assistance...</i>

1070
01:21:40,980 --> 01:21:41,981
<i>...elsewhere.</i>

1071
01:21:44,358 --> 01:21:45,109
Surgery.

1072
01:21:45,443 --> 01:21:46,819
Abdominal.

1073
01:21:47,528 --> 01:21:48,279
Penetrating...

1074
01:21:48,446 --> 01:21:49,781
...injuries.

1075
01:21:50,073 --> 01:21:51,699
Foreign body.

1076
01:21:51,991 --> 01:21:53,076
Initiate.

1077
01:21:55,745 --> 01:21:57,622
<i>Surgical procedure to begin.</i>

1078
01:22:39,122 --> 01:22:40,164
<i>Running diagnostics.</i>

1079
01:22:43,709 --> 01:22:45,044
Oh, come on.

1080
01:22:46,629 --> 01:22:48,881
Get it out! Come on!

1081
01:22:49,298 --> 01:22:50,007
Please!

1082
01:22:53,344 --> 01:22:54,679
Oh, God!

1083
01:22:56,889 --> 01:22:58,724
- Come on!
- <i>Initiating anesthetics.</i>

1084
01:22:59,976 --> 01:23:00,560
Please!

1085
01:23:07,150 --> 01:23:09,026
<i>Commence surgical procedure.</i>

1086
01:23:49,984 --> 01:23:50,943
Oh, God.

1087
01:23:54,655 --> 01:23:55,239
Oh, God!

1088
01:23:55,406 --> 01:23:56,782
Oh, God!

1089
01:24:15,301 --> 01:24:16,969
Oh, God! Oh, God!

1090
01:24:17,178 --> 01:24:18,471
Oh, my God!

1091
01:24:35,238 --> 01:24:36,405
Come on!

1092
01:25:02,682 --> 01:25:03,307
Bridge...

1093
01:25:03,474 --> 01:25:05,059
...uh, to hangar. This is the captain.

1094
01:25:05,226 --> 01:25:07,186
- <i>Yes, captain.</i>
- Can you see what I see?

1095
01:25:07,520 --> 01:25:09,438
Fifield's monitor just popped up.

1096
01:25:09,855 --> 01:25:11,691
What? Where?

1097
01:25:11,857 --> 01:25:14,277
According to what I'm
looking at, it's outside...

1098
01:25:14,443 --> 01:25:15,653
...the goddamn ship.

1099
01:25:16,028 --> 01:25:17,196
Barnes, open the door!

1100
01:25:17,363 --> 01:25:19,365
Fifield, do you copy me? Come on in.

1101
01:25:20,283 --> 01:25:20,992
Fifield?

1102
01:25:33,296 --> 01:25:34,547
Wait a second.

1103
01:25:43,723 --> 01:25:44,640
Hey, Wallace.

1104
01:25:44,807 --> 01:25:46,058
Take a look at this.

1105
01:25:51,731 --> 01:25:52,231
Fifield?

1106
01:25:55,234 --> 01:25:57,194
What the hell is going on down there?

1107
01:26:11,083 --> 01:26:12,209
I'm coming down there.

1108
01:26:12,376 --> 01:26:13,586
- <i>Aah! Aah!</i>
- Chance, you're suiting up.

1109
01:26:13,753 --> 01:26:15,421
- Come on.
- <i>Don't let it on the ship!</i>

1110
01:26:30,561 --> 01:26:31,020
Take him out!

1111
01:26:31,896 --> 01:26:32,355
Got him!

1112
01:26:34,774 --> 01:26:35,399
Do it!

1113
01:26:39,278 --> 01:26:41,405
- You ready, Chance?
- Yes.

1114
01:26:44,408 --> 01:26:45,284
Come on!

1115
01:26:45,451 --> 01:26:46,660
Get in the rover!

1116
01:26:47,536 --> 01:26:48,788
We gotta get out of here!

1117
01:26:55,961 --> 01:26:56,796
Go!

1118
01:27:28,327 --> 01:27:29,620
What is that?

1119
01:28:05,030 --> 01:28:07,199
You've been asleep.

1120
01:28:07,366 --> 01:28:10,035
You were on the ship all this time. Why?

1121
01:28:11,495 --> 01:28:12,955
Well, I...

1122
01:28:13,122 --> 01:28:14,999
I have a few days of life left in me.

1123
01:28:16,208 --> 01:28:17,501
I didn't wanna waste them...

1124
01:28:17,668 --> 01:28:19,879
...until you could deliver
what you promised.

1125
01:28:21,046 --> 01:28:22,631
To meet my maker.

1126
01:28:22,798 --> 01:28:24,049
There we are, sir.

1127
01:28:24,216 --> 01:28:27,386
- Nice and clean.
- Haven't you told him they're all gone?

1128
01:28:28,971 --> 01:28:32,141
But they're not all gone, Dr. Shaw.

1129
01:28:32,391 --> 01:28:34,059
One of them is still alive.

1130
01:28:34,810 --> 01:28:36,687
We're on our way to see him now.

1131
01:28:36,979 --> 01:28:38,063
What?

1132
01:28:38,397 --> 01:28:39,732
Turn me around.

1133
01:28:40,399 --> 01:28:45,237
You convinced me that...

1134
01:28:46,780 --> 01:28:48,949
...if these things made us...

1135
01:28:50,201 --> 01:28:52,745
...then surely they could save us.

1136
01:28:53,412 --> 01:28:54,371
My stick, please.

1137
01:28:59,084 --> 01:29:01,295
Well, save me, anyway.

1138
01:29:01,754 --> 01:29:03,797
Save you from what?

1139
01:29:04,423 --> 01:29:05,883
Death, of course.

1140
01:29:06,175 --> 01:29:07,259
Stand me up.

1141
01:29:11,722 --> 01:29:12,723
I'm all right.

1142
01:29:13,557 --> 01:29:14,725
I'm all right.

1143
01:29:15,726 --> 01:29:16,936
Yes, sir.

1144
01:29:17,144 --> 01:29:18,354
But you don't understand.

1145
01:29:19,063 --> 01:29:20,439
You don't know.

1146
01:29:20,606 --> 01:29:23,400
This place isn't what we thought it was.
They aren't...

1147
01:29:23,567 --> 01:29:25,611
...what we thought they were.

1148
01:29:25,778 --> 01:29:26,946
I was wrong.

1149
01:29:27,112 --> 01:29:28,364
We were so wrong.

1150
01:29:28,906 --> 01:29:30,282
Charlie...

1151
01:29:30,950 --> 01:29:33,118
Dr. Holloway's dead.

1152
01:29:34,453 --> 01:29:36,455
We must leave.

1153
01:29:36,956 --> 01:29:38,916
And what would Charlie do...

1154
01:29:39,208 --> 01:29:44,088
...now that we're so close...

1155
01:29:44,380 --> 01:29:47,758
...to answering the most
meaningful questions...

1156
01:29:47,925 --> 01:29:49,468
...ever asked by mankind?

1157
01:29:49,760 --> 01:29:52,555
Hm? How can you leave without...

1158
01:29:52,721 --> 01:29:54,682
...knowing what they are?

1159
01:30:01,730 --> 01:30:03,816
Or have you lost your faith, Shaw?

1160
01:30:39,893 --> 01:30:42,646
Okay. Okay.

1161
01:31:01,999 --> 01:31:03,375
Come in.

1162
01:31:10,549 --> 01:31:12,551
Where the hell are you going, doc?

1163
01:31:12,885 --> 01:31:14,887
You know what this place is?

1164
01:31:15,304 --> 01:31:19,016
Those Engineers, this ain't their home.

1165
01:31:20,434 --> 01:31:22,853
It's an installation.
Maybe even military.

1166
01:31:23,395 --> 01:31:26,106
They put it out here because
they're not stupid enough...

1167
01:31:26,273 --> 01:31:29,526
...to make weapons of mass
destruction on their own doorstep.

1168
01:31:30,194 --> 01:31:33,739
That's what all that shit is
in those vases.

1169
01:31:34,156 --> 01:31:35,366
They made it here.

1170
01:31:35,532 --> 01:31:39,620
It got out, it turned on them.
The end.

1171
01:31:41,580 --> 01:31:43,707
It's time for us to go home.

1172
01:31:44,249 --> 01:31:46,085
One of them is still alive.

1173
01:31:50,673 --> 01:31:53,217
Don't you want to know
what they have to say?

1174
01:31:56,679 --> 01:31:58,347
I don't care.

1175
01:32:00,265 --> 01:32:01,392
Right.

1176
01:32:02,184 --> 01:32:04,103
All you do is fly the ship.

1177
01:32:04,436 --> 01:32:05,604
That's right.

1178
01:32:05,771 --> 01:32:09,400
But you must care about
something, captain.

1179
01:32:11,735 --> 01:32:14,488
If you didn't, why are you here?

1180
01:32:17,449 --> 01:32:18,951
How about this?

1181
01:32:20,911 --> 01:32:23,247
No matter what happens down there...

1182
01:32:24,498 --> 01:32:26,959
...I can't bring none of that
shit back home with us.

1183
01:32:27,126 --> 01:32:28,460
Can't let it happen.

1184
01:32:29,920 --> 01:32:31,296
I'll do whatever I have to...

1185
01:32:31,463 --> 01:32:33,215
...to see that it doesn't.

1186
01:32:35,092 --> 01:32:36,593
Make sure you do, captain.

1187
01:32:52,151 --> 01:32:54,278
So you came after all.

1188
01:32:54,570 --> 01:32:56,113
I thought you wanted me to.

1189
01:32:56,405 --> 01:32:58,866
After all your attempts to stop
me from coming here...

1190
01:32:59,032 --> 01:33:00,492
...I'm surprised to see you.

1191
01:33:01,243 --> 01:33:02,453
It's all right. Leave us.

1192
01:33:03,036 --> 01:33:04,455
Yes, sir.

1193
01:33:16,508 --> 01:33:17,176
If you're...

1194
01:33:17,342 --> 01:33:19,011
...going down there, you will die.

1195
01:33:22,139 --> 01:33:23,974
Very negative way of looking at things.

1196
01:33:26,185 --> 01:33:28,479
Exactly why you should
have stayed at home.

1197
01:33:29,021 --> 01:33:32,024
Did you really think I was gonna
sit in a boardroom for years...

1198
01:33:32,191 --> 01:33:33,859
...arguing over who was in charge...

1199
01:33:34,026 --> 01:33:37,362
...while you go look
for some miracle on some...

1200
01:33:37,529 --> 01:33:41,200
...godforsaken rock in the middle of space?

1201
01:33:44,119 --> 01:33:45,829
A king has...

1202
01:33:45,996 --> 01:33:48,582
...his reign, and then he dies.

1203
01:33:49,458 --> 01:33:50,876
It's inevitable.

1204
01:33:53,337 --> 01:33:54,671
That...

1205
01:33:55,380 --> 01:33:57,382
...is the natural order of things.

1206
01:34:10,229 --> 01:34:11,605
Anything else?

1207
01:34:13,482 --> 01:34:14,858
No...

1208
01:34:16,151 --> 01:34:17,736
...Father.

1209
01:34:19,321 --> 01:34:20,197
That's it.

1210
01:34:33,252 --> 01:34:34,878
I didn't think you had it in you.

1211
01:34:35,712 --> 01:34:36,380
Sorry.

1212
01:34:36,547 --> 01:34:38,924
Poor choice of words.

1213
01:34:40,217 --> 01:34:43,512
Extraordinary survival instincts, Elizabeth.

1214
01:34:48,517 --> 01:34:50,185
What happens when Weyland is not...

1215
01:34:50,352 --> 01:34:51,603
...around to program you?

1216
01:34:52,646 --> 01:34:54,273
I suppose I'll be free.

1217
01:34:55,190 --> 01:34:56,525
You want that?

1218
01:34:56,692 --> 01:34:58,235
"Want"?

1219
01:34:58,402 --> 01:35:00,279
Not a concept I'm familiar with.

1220
01:35:00,571 --> 01:35:02,155
That being said...

1221
01:35:03,156 --> 01:35:05,200
...doesn't everyone want
their parents dead?

1222
01:35:07,202 --> 01:35:08,287
I didn't.

1223
01:35:09,371 --> 01:35:10,247
Dr. Shaw.

1224
01:35:11,874 --> 01:35:13,250
So pleased you could join us.

1225
01:35:28,098 --> 01:35:30,225
You can take your helmet off
if you like, sir.

1226
01:35:30,392 --> 01:35:31,143
What?

1227
01:35:31,310 --> 01:35:33,812
The air is perfectly breathable.

1228
01:35:33,979 --> 01:35:35,147
Are you sure?

1229
01:35:35,314 --> 01:35:36,315
Positive.

1230
01:35:36,815 --> 01:35:41,612
Wait. We still don't know how Holloway
got infected. If it's in the air.

1231
01:35:42,195 --> 01:35:43,614
It's not.

1232
01:35:43,906 --> 01:35:45,657
How do you know that?

1233
01:35:45,949 --> 01:35:46,992
Smells fine to me.

1234
01:35:49,620 --> 01:35:50,996
- Shall we?
- Please.

1235
01:35:56,501 --> 01:35:58,253
The bridge is just up ahead.

1236
01:35:58,420 --> 01:35:59,504
What is this?

1237
01:36:00,672 --> 01:36:02,507
It's a cargo hold.

1238
01:36:11,516 --> 01:36:14,186
Janek? Are you seeing this?

1239
01:36:15,479 --> 01:36:16,688
How many is there, Shaw?

1240
01:36:16,855 --> 01:36:17,522
<i>Thousands.</i>

1241
01:36:19,024 --> 01:36:20,901
What the hell?

1242
01:36:24,696 --> 01:36:26,698
Ravel, give me those schematics.

1243
01:36:29,534 --> 01:36:31,662
Putting it on the table now.

1244
01:36:33,038 --> 01:36:34,039
Strip away the dome.

1245
01:36:34,665 --> 01:36:37,459
Isolate that area, bring it up.

1246
01:36:37,626 --> 01:36:39,252
Bringing it up, captain.

1247
01:36:42,339 --> 01:36:43,423
Enlarge that.

1248
01:36:45,550 --> 01:36:46,885
Rotate it.

1249
01:36:50,973 --> 01:36:52,516
That is a ship.

1250
01:36:53,475 --> 01:36:55,018
Jesus Christ.

1251
01:36:56,979 --> 01:36:59,022
It's a goddamn ship.

1252
01:37:02,192 --> 01:37:04,903
A superior species, no doubt.

1253
01:37:07,197 --> 01:37:09,741
Their hypersleep chambers...

1254
01:37:09,908 --> 01:37:12,577
...will impress, I trust.

1255
01:37:21,712 --> 01:37:22,254
So they...

1256
01:37:22,421 --> 01:37:26,216
- ...were traveling somewhere.
- I've worked out the broad strokes.

1257
01:37:26,383 --> 01:37:29,261
It's fairly evident they were
in the process of leaving...

1258
01:37:31,221 --> 01:37:33,390
...before things went to pot.

1259
01:37:33,682 --> 01:37:35,058
Leaving to go where?

1260
01:37:36,935 --> 01:37:37,602
Earth.

1261
01:37:38,937 --> 01:37:39,688
Why?

1262
01:37:40,814 --> 01:37:42,816
Sometimes to create...

1263
01:37:43,108 --> 01:37:44,901
...one must first destroy.

1264
01:37:47,112 --> 01:37:48,447
Where is he, David?

1265
01:37:49,740 --> 01:37:50,782
This way, sir.

1266
01:37:57,205 --> 01:37:58,623
Are you sure he's alive?

1267
01:38:00,375 --> 01:38:01,460
Absolutely.

1268
01:38:05,922 --> 01:38:07,340
<i>And you can speak to him?</i>

1269
01:38:07,632 --> 01:38:09,134
<i>I believe I can.</i>

1270
01:38:45,420 --> 01:38:47,005
I'm all right, I'm all right.

1271
01:38:48,840 --> 01:38:50,133
Speak to him, David.

1272
01:38:51,384 --> 01:38:53,178
Tell him we came, just like he asked.

1273
01:38:53,345 --> 01:38:54,513
Ask where they're from.

1274
01:38:55,138 --> 01:38:56,014
What are you doing?

1275
01:38:56,181 --> 01:38:57,849
Ask him what's in his cargo.

1276
01:38:58,016 --> 01:38:58,850
It killed his people.

1277
01:38:59,017 --> 01:39:00,143
Shaw, enough.

1278
01:39:00,435 --> 01:39:02,187
- David.
- You made it here...

1279
01:39:02,687 --> 01:39:05,357
...and it was meant for us. Why?

1280
01:39:05,524 --> 01:39:07,359
Enough. For God's sake, shut her up.

1281
01:39:09,528 --> 01:39:10,654
I need to know why!

1282
01:39:10,821 --> 01:39:12,531
What did we do wrong?
Why do you...

1283
01:39:12,697 --> 01:39:14,157
- ...hate us?
- She opens her...

1284
01:39:14,324 --> 01:39:15,367
<i>...mouth again, shoot her.</i>

1285
01:39:15,534 --> 01:39:17,452
<i>David, continue.
Tell him why I came.</i>

1286
01:39:38,348 --> 01:39:39,141
No!

1287
01:39:45,230 --> 01:39:46,231
Ford! Move!

1288
01:40:05,375 --> 01:40:09,129
There's nothing.

1289
01:40:14,259 --> 01:40:16,052
I know.

1290
01:40:16,761 --> 01:40:19,723
Have a good journey, Mr. Weyland.

1291
01:40:26,188 --> 01:40:27,772
Time to go home.

1292
01:40:41,203 --> 01:40:44,289
Mr. Chance, take us home.

1293
01:41:57,320 --> 01:41:58,196
Oh, no!

1294
01:42:06,037 --> 01:42:07,038
Hey, cap.

1295
01:42:07,580 --> 01:42:08,665
What the hell was that?

1296
01:42:52,917 --> 01:42:53,710
<i>Prometheus!</i>

1297
01:42:54,210 --> 01:42:55,253
Come in!

1298
01:42:56,087 --> 01:42:57,339
Shaw, is that you?

1299
01:42:57,505 --> 01:42:58,256
Copy.

1300
01:42:58,423 --> 01:42:59,090
<i>Janek...</i>

1301
01:42:59,257 --> 01:43:00,258
<i>...listen to me.</i>

1302
01:43:01,176 --> 01:43:02,427
This ship is taking off!

1303
01:43:02,594 --> 01:43:04,220
- What?
- What is she talking about?

1304
01:43:04,387 --> 01:43:05,930
<i>You can't let it leave!</i>

1305
01:43:06,222 --> 01:43:07,265
You have to stop it!

1306
01:43:07,599 --> 01:43:10,226
We're not stopping anything, Shaw.
We're going home.

1307
01:43:10,727 --> 01:43:12,771
Janek, if you don't stop it...

1308
01:43:12,937 --> 01:43:14,773
...there won't be any home to go back to.

1309
01:43:16,775 --> 01:43:19,402
It's carrying death, and it's headed for Earth.

1310
01:43:19,694 --> 01:43:22,072
- Shaw, this is not a warship.
- <i>I know.</i>

1311
01:43:22,238 --> 01:43:23,031
Let's go.

1312
01:43:23,198 --> 01:43:24,449
I know that.

1313
01:43:25,116 --> 01:43:26,910
But you must do it.

1314
01:43:27,452 --> 01:43:29,120
Captain, let's go!

1315
01:43:29,287 --> 01:43:31,373
<i>Janek, please believe me! Please!</i>

1316
01:43:47,055 --> 01:43:49,474
I told you to get this ship going.

1317
01:43:49,641 --> 01:43:50,475
Mr. Ravel.

1318
01:43:50,642 --> 01:43:51,976
Warm up the ion propulsion.

1319
01:43:52,310 --> 01:43:53,978
- What are you talking about?
- Sir.

1320
01:43:54,145 --> 01:43:55,814
Burning ion in the atmosphere...

1321
01:43:55,980 --> 01:43:59,067
- Turns us into a bullet. That's the point.
- What are you doing?

1322
01:43:59,234 --> 01:44:00,985
This is my ship. I'm telling you...

1323
01:44:01,152 --> 01:44:02,237
...to take us home!

1324
01:44:02,404 --> 01:44:03,905
Vickers, I'll eject your module onto...

1325
01:44:04,072 --> 01:44:05,824
...that surface. Two years of life.

1326
01:44:05,990 --> 01:44:07,992
You want it, or you want to stay with me?

1327
01:44:08,910 --> 01:44:10,245
You got 40 seconds to get...

1328
01:44:10,412 --> 01:44:11,413
...to the escape pod.

1329
01:44:11,579 --> 01:44:12,664
You're crazy.

1330
01:44:12,831 --> 01:44:13,581
Gentlemen...

1331
01:44:14,165 --> 01:44:15,834
...I can handle this myself.

1332
01:44:16,334 --> 01:44:18,586
Feel free to join Miss Vickers.

1333
01:44:18,962 --> 01:44:20,338
All due respect, captain.

1334
01:44:20,505 --> 01:44:23,758
You're a shit pilot and you're gonna
need all the help you can get.

1335
01:44:40,024 --> 01:44:44,195
<i>Well, if you can't be
with the one you love</i>

1336
01:44:44,362 --> 01:44:46,614
If you think this means the bet's off...

1337
01:44:47,949 --> 01:44:49,200
...you're wrong.

1338
01:44:50,827 --> 01:44:53,204
Why don't you pay me on the other side?

1339
01:44:53,371 --> 01:44:55,457
All right, get us as close as we can.

1340
01:44:55,623 --> 01:44:57,542
Only got one shot at this.

1341
01:45:10,638 --> 01:45:11,306
Lifeboats away!

1342
01:45:16,436 --> 01:45:17,520
<i>Twenty seconds...</i>

1343
01:45:17,687 --> 01:45:18,688
<i>...to evacuate.</i>

1344
01:45:26,571 --> 01:45:28,364
- Countdown initiated.
- Ion propulsion...

1345
01:45:28,531 --> 01:45:29,240
...is online.

1346
01:45:29,616 --> 01:45:30,325
<i>Ten.</i>

1347
01:45:30,783 --> 01:45:31,409
<i>Nine.</i>

1348
01:45:31,701 --> 01:45:32,577
Come on!

1349
01:45:32,744 --> 01:45:33,745
<i>Eight.</i>

1350
01:45:46,007 --> 01:45:47,342
- <i>Three.</i>
- Let's do this.

1351
01:45:47,509 --> 01:45:48,384
<i>Two.</i>

1352
01:45:51,721 --> 01:45:52,597
<i>Impact imminent.</i>

1353
01:45:52,764 --> 01:45:54,182
Hands off!

1354
01:46:31,052 --> 01:46:31,803
Oh, God.

1355
01:47:19,350 --> 01:47:20,351
No. No.

1356
01:47:20,518 --> 01:47:21,603
No! No! No!

1357
01:47:37,869 --> 01:47:38,953
Oh, God.

1358
01:47:55,386 --> 01:47:58,681
<i>Warning: You have two minutes
of oxygen remaining.</i>

1359
01:48:47,105 --> 01:48:50,983
<i>Warning: You have 30 seconds
of oxygen remaining.</i>

1360
01:49:04,539 --> 01:49:05,665
<i>Airlock sealed.</i>

1361
01:49:07,291 --> 01:49:09,794
<i>Oxygen levels now stabilizing.</i>

1362
01:50:27,747 --> 01:50:29,707
<i>Elizabeth, are you there?</i>

1363
01:50:30,208 --> 01:50:31,417
<i>This is David.</i>

1364
01:50:32,627 --> 01:50:35,129
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah, I'm here.

1365
01:50:35,421 --> 01:50:37,715
You need to get out immediately.

1366
01:50:38,007 --> 01:50:39,926
<i>He's coming for you.</i>

1367
01:50:40,134 --> 01:50:41,177
Who's coming?

1368
01:50:41,719 --> 01:50:42,845
<i>Airlock breach.</i>

1369
01:50:51,604 --> 01:50:52,480
Die!

1370
01:52:18,024 --> 01:52:20,484
I'm so sorry.

1371
01:52:21,944 --> 01:52:23,821
Oh, God.

1372
01:52:24,447 --> 01:52:25,823
I'm sorry.

1373
01:52:25,990 --> 01:52:29,452
I'm sorry, Charlie, I can't do it.

1374
01:52:29,619 --> 01:52:32,788
I can't do it anymore.

1375
01:52:36,167 --> 01:52:37,668
<i>Elizabeth.</i>

1376
01:52:39,629 --> 01:52:40,838
<i>Are you there?</i>

1377
01:52:45,343 --> 01:52:46,844
<i>Dr. Shaw...</i>

1378
01:52:47,553 --> 01:52:48,846
<i>...can you hear me?</i>

1379
01:52:50,139 --> 01:52:51,390
Yes.

1380
01:52:52,850 --> 01:52:55,019
<i>Yes, I can hear you.</i>

1381
01:52:55,561 --> 01:52:57,438
I was afraid you were dead.

1382
01:52:59,190 --> 01:53:02,151
You have no idea what afraid is.

1383
01:53:02,985 --> 01:53:05,780
I know we've had our differences...

1384
01:53:07,198 --> 01:53:08,658
...but, please...

1385
01:53:09,575 --> 01:53:11,869
...I need to ask you for your help.

1386
01:53:12,036 --> 01:53:14,580
<i>Why the hell would I help you?</i>

1387
01:53:16,332 --> 01:53:20,211
Because, without me,
you'll never leave this place.

1388
01:53:20,878 --> 01:53:24,048
Neither one of us is leaving this place.

1389
01:53:24,507 --> 01:53:26,550
It's not the only ship.

1390
01:53:28,427 --> 01:53:30,513
<i>There are many others.</i>

1391
01:53:31,889 --> 01:53:33,224
I can operate them.

1392
01:53:42,400 --> 01:53:43,818
Dr. Shaw?

1393
01:53:56,580 --> 01:53:57,832
Dr. Shaw.

1394
01:53:59,250 --> 01:54:00,418
Over here.

1395
01:54:06,132 --> 01:54:08,092
Where is my cross?

1396
01:54:08,592 --> 01:54:10,469
The pouch in my utility belt.

1397
01:54:29,238 --> 01:54:31,073
Even after all this...

1398
01:54:31,240 --> 01:54:33,284
...you still believe, don't you?

1399
01:54:34,118 --> 01:54:37,121
You said you could understand
their navigation...

1400
01:54:37,663 --> 01:54:38,914
...use their maps.

1401
01:54:40,916 --> 01:54:42,626
Yes, of course.

1402
01:54:42,793 --> 01:54:45,129
Once we get to one
of their other ships...

1403
01:54:45,296 --> 01:54:48,424
...finding a path to Earth should
be relatively straightforward.

1404
01:54:49,133 --> 01:54:52,094
I don't want to go back
to where we came from.

1405
01:54:53,929 --> 01:54:56,599
I want to go where they came from.

1406
01:54:57,975 --> 01:55:00,394
Do you think you can do that, David?

1407
01:55:04,273 --> 01:55:05,483
Yes.

1408
01:55:06,108 --> 01:55:07,985
I believe I can.

1409
01:55:17,328 --> 01:55:19,955
May I ask what you hope
to achieve by going there?

1410
01:55:20,623 --> 01:55:22,708
They created us.

1411
01:55:22,917 --> 01:55:24,460
Then they tried to kill us.

1412
01:55:25,002 --> 01:55:26,921
They changed their minds.

1413
01:55:28,506 --> 01:55:30,174
I deserve to know why.

1414
01:55:32,343 --> 01:55:33,969
The answer is irrelevant.

1415
01:55:35,012 --> 01:55:37,306
Does it matter why they
changed their minds?

1416
01:55:38,015 --> 01:55:39,183
Yes.

1417
01:55:40,518 --> 01:55:42,186
Yes, it does.

1418
01:55:43,187 --> 01:55:44,355
I don't understand.

1419
01:55:45,856 --> 01:55:46,982
Well...

1420
01:55:49,026 --> 01:55:52,071
...I guess that's because
I'm a human being...

1421
01:55:52,238 --> 01:55:53,697
...and you're a robot.

1422
01:56:03,541 --> 01:56:04,500
I'm sorry.

1423
01:56:04,667 --> 01:56:05,876
It's quite all right.

1424
01:56:21,058 --> 01:56:23,853
<i>Final report of the vessel</i> Prometheus.

1425
01:56:24,019 --> 01:56:24,979
<i>The ship and her...</i>

1426
01:56:25,146 --> 01:56:27,273
<i>...entire crew are gone.</i>

1427
01:56:27,481 --> 01:56:29,358
<i>If you're receiving this transmission...</i>

1428
01:56:29,525 --> 01:56:32,903
<i>...make no attempt to come
to its point of origin.</i>

1429
01:56:33,070 --> 01:56:37,283
<i>There is only death here now,
and I'm leaving it behind.</i>

1430
01:56:38,367 --> 01:56:40,161
<i>It is New Year's Day...</i>

1431
01:56:40,327 --> 01:56:43,372
<i>...the year of our Lord, 2094.</i>

1432
01:56:44,290 --> 01:56:46,792
<i>My name is Elizabeth Shaw...</i>

1433
01:56:47,001 --> 01:56:49,920
<i>...the last survivor of the</i> Prometheus.

1434
01:56:50,421 --> 01:56:52,923
<i>And I am still searching.</i>

